1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:11,933
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:38,467 --> 00:00:41,267
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:41,367 --> 00:00:42,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:47,000
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:57,433
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,533 --> 00:00:59,267
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,367 --> 00:01:00,567
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:00,667 --> 00:01:01,933
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:04,000
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,367 --> 00:01:07,333
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:09,867 --> 00:01:12,633
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:17,200
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,333 --> 00:01:19,833
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,633
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:25,033
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,167 --> 00:01:28,033
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:31,967
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:32,067 --> 00:01:34,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:34,833 --> 00:01:35,800
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:35,967 --> 00:01:37,433
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,533 --> 00:01:38,633
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:38,733 --> 00:01:41,033
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:45,833 --> 00:01:51,367
<i>We caught a big fish,
the gold smuggling ringleader,</i>

24
00:01:51,533 --> 00:01:54,700
<i> Victor Zafra, alias "Tiger."</i>

25
00:01:54,867 --> 00:01:57,067
<i>You guys got lucky.
The only reason you got me</i>

26
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,033
<i>was because of that guy
who was chasing me.</i>

27
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:02,967
<i>What's Zafra talking about?
Who is that guy?</i>

28
00:02:03,067 --> 00:02:05,167
<i>I think he's also one of
Zafra's enemies.</i>

29
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:07,700
<i> Find out who that guy is.</i>

30
00:02:07,867 --> 00:02:09,200
<i> That woman is at fault here.</i>

31
00:02:09,367 --> 00:02:10,400
<i> Who is she anyway?</i>

32
00:02:10,533 --> 00:02:12,200
<i>She has no idea
who she's messing with.</i>

33
00:02:12,367 --> 00:02:14,233
<i>You guys know I'm the one
who finished Rudy off.</i>

34
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:15,667
<i> Betchay might find out.</i>

35
00:02:15,767 --> 00:02:20,900
<i>I hired Betchay so we can use
her as leverage against Gabo</i>

36
00:02:21,067 --> 00:02:22,400
<i> in case things get messy.</i>

37
00:02:22,567 --> 00:02:25,867
<i>You'll bring Tiger's head
to Pops.</i>

38
00:02:26,033 --> 00:02:30,200
<i>But you failed, so we're not
paying you anything.</i>

39
00:02:30,367 --> 00:02:33,033
<i>You guys just
played me for a fool.</i>

40
00:02:33,133 --> 00:02:34,700
<i> You're all full of crap.</i>

41
00:02:34,867 --> 00:02:36,167
[FIST SLAMS TABLE]

42
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:47,567
<i> Pancit</i> (Stir-fried noodles)
for Pops!

43
00:02:47,767 --> 00:02:48,867
Pops!

44
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:52,767
Thank you.

45
00:02:52,933 --> 00:02:55,400
How's Gabo's mission?

46
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:56,567
Well, Pops,

47
00:02:56,667 --> 00:03:00,267
he was so sure
he'd arrest him, but... fail!

48
00:03:00,433 --> 00:03:01,933
He didn't see Tiger?

49
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:05,700
Zero. Nada.
Gabo blew the whole thing, Pops!

50
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,400
What happened
in Chinatown?

51
00:03:07,567 --> 00:03:11,567
Gabo said he almost
caught Tiger.

52
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:13,567
He was even bragging, Pops.

53
00:03:13,733 --> 00:03:17,067
He said he took down
Tiger's men.

54
00:03:17,167 --> 00:03:19,867
So arrogant.

55
00:03:19,967 --> 00:03:23,100
Suddenly, someone fired shots,
so he had to escape.

56
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:26,100
- Who fired?
- Probably Tiger's men.

57
00:03:26,267 --> 00:03:30,733
Pops, I think Gabo
is just making excuses.

58
00:03:30,833 --> 00:03:33,167
[OMENG] Pops,
you need to see this.

59
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:37,933
It's on the news.
Tiger's been caught.

60
00:03:40,267 --> 00:03:42,567
[DELGADO]<i> A big fish
</i> has been caught:

61
00:03:42,667 --> 00:03:45,800
<i> the gold smuggling ringleader,</i>

62
00:03:45,967 --> 00:03:48,900
<i> Victor Zafra, alias "Tiger."</i>

63
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,400
<i>The exploitation of our
natural resources</i>

64
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:55,767
<i>and the theft from our nation
will finally stop</i>

65
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:58,467
<i> because of his arrest.</i>

66
00:03:58,567 --> 00:04:00,933
<i>And I am proud to announce
tonight</i>

67
00:04:01,033 --> 00:04:05,333
<i>that this arrest would not
be possible</i>

68
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:12,200
<i>if not for the NCIA agents
led by Sam Jacinto.</i>

69
00:04:12,333 --> 00:04:15,467
So Tiger's been caught.

70
00:04:15,567 --> 00:04:18,133
The NCIA got him.

71
00:04:18,233 --> 00:04:20,833
They're probably the ones
who shot at Gabo.

72
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,700
It would've been better
if we had Tiger.

73
00:04:23,833 --> 00:04:26,633
Just watch. That bastard
will get out in no time.

74
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:30,467
[UWAK] With his money and
his family's influence,

75
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:31,867
they can easily buy
his freedom.

76
00:04:32,033 --> 00:04:33,800
He'll just buy his way out.

77
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:37,800
And once he's out, it'll be
harder to catch him again.

78
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:44,000
Let it go. What matters is
Tiger is behind bars for now.

79
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:47,033
Tomas.

80
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:50,133
Looks like someone lost a bet.

81
00:04:51,767 --> 00:04:55,833
Hey man, if you get any CCTV
footage of that guy I fought,

82
00:04:55,933 --> 00:04:57,900
give it to me right away.

83
00:04:58,033 --> 00:04:59,967
[REYES] Sure. I got you.

84
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,033
Thanks, man.

85
00:05:04,133 --> 00:05:05,600
- Tuazon.
- Hm?

86
00:05:05,733 --> 00:05:07,700
Why are you investigating
that guy?

87
00:05:07,867 --> 00:05:10,233
Why do you think?

88
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:12,533
He messed up our mission,
obviously.

89
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:15,367
And besides that,
he kissed you, didn't he?

90
00:05:15,467 --> 00:05:18,700
Can you please just drop it?
I'll handle it myself.

91
00:05:18,867 --> 00:05:20,200
Why shouldn't I look into it?

92
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:23,400
I'm doing this for you,
to get back at him.

93
00:05:23,567 --> 00:05:26,700
Hold on. I don't need you to
get revenge or protect me.

94
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,367
Did you forget?

95
00:05:28,533 --> 00:05:30,533
Because of your
little fistfight,

96
00:05:30,633 --> 00:05:32,567
our mission was almost blown.

97
00:05:34,333 --> 00:05:36,267
So now you're taking his side?

98
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:40,400
Wow... what a flirt.

99
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:42,367
Excuse me, ma'am?

100
00:05:42,467 --> 00:05:46,067
[SEBASTIAN] I'm trying to
protect you, and you're mad?

101
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:50,733
Hold on a second.
Let me remind you,

102
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:54,200
I've said it before: I don't
need your protection.

103
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:56,600
That guy is mine.

104
00:05:56,767 --> 00:05:58,900
He's my problem, okay?

105
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:05,633
[BROODING MUSIC PLAYING]

106
00:06:05,767 --> 00:06:08,200
What are you guys watching?

107
00:06:08,333 --> 00:06:11,600
Taxpayers don't pay us to
watch our coworkers, okay?

108
00:06:11,767 --> 00:06:14,267
Oh, my desk is over there.

109
00:06:18,133 --> 00:06:19,500
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

110
00:06:19,633 --> 00:06:22,100
[MUSIC FADES]

111
00:06:39,467 --> 00:06:46,433
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

112
00:06:48,967 --> 00:06:51,667
- Hand it over! Come on!
- No! Please, no!

113
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:54,433
- Please, don't.
- Stab her right now!

114
00:06:54,567 --> 00:06:58,267
Please, have mercy!
I need this money

115
00:06:58,400 --> 00:06:59,800
- for my husband's surgery.
- Hand it over.

116
00:06:59,967 --> 00:07:01,433
- Give us the money now!
- [YELPS] Stop it!

117
00:07:01,567 --> 00:07:03,700
- I'll give it to you!
- Hand it over!

118
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:08,767
- Give it up!
- [BETCHAY WHIMPERS]

119
00:07:08,867 --> 00:07:10,633
Ouch! I can't give this up...

120
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:13,700
It's for my husband's surgery.

121
00:07:13,833 --> 00:07:15,600
- Ma!
- Gabo!

122
00:07:15,733 --> 00:07:16,833
- Gabo!
- Gabo, help me!

123
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,233
- Stay out of this!
- Gabo!

124
00:07:18,367 --> 00:07:20,067
- We need the money!
- I'm being robbed!

125
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:22,367
[SOBBING]
Gabo, help me!

126
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:25,467
If you don't let go of
my mother...

127
00:07:25,567 --> 00:07:28,400
and return her money...

128
00:07:28,533 --> 00:07:29,733
the three of you...

129
00:07:29,867 --> 00:07:32,800
I'll make sure they hold your
funerals tomorrow morning.

130
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:34,233
[BLADES UNSHEATHING]

131
00:07:34,367 --> 00:07:35,800
Gabo! We don't want trouble!

132
00:07:35,933 --> 00:07:38,733
We're giving back your
mother's money!

133
00:07:38,867 --> 00:07:40,567
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

134
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:45,133
[BETCHAY WHIMPERS]

135
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:49,367
Ma?

136
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:56,000
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

137
00:07:56,133 --> 00:07:57,533
[BLADES SHEATHING]

138
00:07:57,700 --> 00:07:59,700
[PAPER RUSTLING]

139
00:07:59,867 --> 00:08:01,833
Ma... Ma!

140
00:08:01,967 --> 00:08:06,733
- [SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [BETCHAY SOBS SOFTLY]

141
00:08:06,867 --> 00:08:08,333
Don't touch me!

142
00:08:08,433 --> 00:08:10,367
I didn't need your help at all!

143
00:08:10,533 --> 00:08:12,933
I could've handled those
punks myself!

144
00:08:13,067 --> 00:08:14,333
You're so annoying.

145
00:08:18,233 --> 00:08:25,067
[MUSIC BECOMES EMOTIONAL]

146
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:32,367
[RALLOS CLEARS THROAT]

147
00:08:32,467 --> 00:08:33,600
Ah, sir.

148
00:08:34,333 --> 00:08:37,467
Looks like
Ma'am Sam keeps rejecting you.

149
00:08:37,633 --> 00:08:39,033
She's just playing hard to get.

150
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:44,400
- Jacinto will be mine someday.
- I know that, sir,

151
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:47,600
because I know you have
a lot of hidden techniques.

152
00:08:47,767 --> 00:08:51,133
I mean, others do
prohibited techniques, you know?

153
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:52,433
Come here, Rallos.

154
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:56,733
You know, what I like most...

155
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,967
...is something
that challenges me.

156
00:09:00,667 --> 00:09:02,800
Something that gives me
a very hard time.

157
00:09:03,933 --> 00:09:05,300
That's what I like.

158
00:09:05,433 --> 00:09:07,833
And what Jacinto's doing
to me...

159
00:09:09,033 --> 00:09:11,100
...is making me lose my sanity!

160
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:15,267
Don't worry.
Jacinto will be mine.

161
00:09:15,367 --> 00:09:16,833
That's why you're my idol, sir.

162
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:17,933
[FISTS BUMP]

163
00:09:19,967 --> 00:09:20,967
[PIA] Sam!

164
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:24,000
[PIA BREATHES]

165
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:29,600
Oh, why does it seem
like your mood's heavy

166
00:09:29,733 --> 00:09:32,667
despite a successful mission?

167
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:35,767
But is it really
mission accomplished?

168
00:09:37,167 --> 00:09:38,633
Is there something
you would like to ask?

169
00:09:38,733 --> 00:09:41,033
There is! Um...

170
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:44,300
But I won't ask you.
I'll ask your agents.

171
00:09:45,067 --> 00:09:48,200
I'll review your case
because it's too messy!

172
00:09:48,833 --> 00:09:51,533
A lot of NCIA agents
were injured.

173
00:09:52,233 --> 00:09:53,767
Like you just abandoned them.

174
00:09:54,700 --> 00:09:56,667
It's like...
[SMACKS LIPS]

175
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:58,433
You weren't prepared.

176
00:09:59,733 --> 00:10:02,300
Ma'am Pia, it's not true
that we weren't prepared.

177
00:10:02,433 --> 00:10:04,700
Accidents are inevitable
in an operation.

178
00:10:04,833 --> 00:10:06,700
Don't explain.

179
00:10:06,867 --> 00:10:09,333
I'm just telling you
I'm going to investigate.

180
00:10:10,367 --> 00:10:11,700
So you won't be surprised!

181
00:10:13,033 --> 00:10:14,900
I'm nice enough, see?

182
00:10:15,533 --> 00:10:16,900
I gave you a heads-up.

183
00:10:18,433 --> 00:10:19,400
[PIA SCOFFS]

184
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:27,900
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

185
00:10:31,767 --> 00:10:33,000
[DOOR OPENS]

186
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:34,867
- Ma'am Sam.
- How did it go?

187
00:10:35,033 --> 00:10:37,100
The man we were after escaped.

188
00:10:37,233 --> 00:10:39,600
- Did you see his face?
- No, ma'am. I'm sorry.

189
00:10:39,767 --> 00:10:42,567
He got away?
Who could that man be?

190
00:10:43,867 --> 00:10:47,933
I don't know who he is.
But I know he ruined our plan.

191
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:51,700
I'll make sure I'll find out
who he is.

192
00:10:58,300 --> 00:10:59,200
Woo!

193
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:00,833
[CHUCKLING, CLAPPING]

194
00:11:00,967 --> 00:11:02,933
- Woo!
- [UWAK CHCUKLING]

195
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:05,267
- How about that?
- Well?

196
00:11:05,967 --> 00:11:07,900
- Well?
- Well?

197
00:11:08,067 --> 00:11:10,200
- Give it!
- You lost the bet!

198
00:11:10,333 --> 00:11:12,533
- You just got lucky.
- [UWAK CHUCKLING]

199
00:11:12,667 --> 00:11:15,533
- And Gabo was just unlucky!
- [LAWIN] Hmm.

200
00:11:15,667 --> 00:11:20,533
No one's lucky or unlucky.
We know Gabo!

201
00:11:20,667 --> 00:11:23,933
He's a bit good.
Just a bit, okay?

202
00:11:24,067 --> 00:11:25,567
But he has no strategy.

203
00:11:25,667 --> 00:11:27,733
He'll be better
in the mission.

204
00:11:27,833 --> 00:11:29,400
That is if there's a next one.

205
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:32,300
That is if Pops will give him
another chance.

206
00:11:32,467 --> 00:11:33,767
You just got lucky.

207
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:34,967
- Give it!
- Give it!

208
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:36,467
- Pay up!
- [OMENG] Fine, fine.

209
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:38,467
There's no such thing as luck.

210
00:11:39,333 --> 00:11:40,967
Mm-hmm!

211
00:11:46,033 --> 00:11:46,900
[DOOR OPENS]

212
00:11:47,033 --> 00:11:49,833
[ARTURO] Ma'am, sir.
Attorney is here.

213
00:11:50,533 --> 00:11:51,467
Attorney.

214
00:11:56,933 --> 00:11:59,167
Attorney, find a way

215
00:11:59,333 --> 00:12:01,833
to get Victor
out of jail right now.

216
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
- I'll try, ma'am.
- What?

217
00:12:04,967 --> 00:12:09,133
You'll try? Don't just try.
Do it!

218
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,300
We pay you so much,
so do your job!

219
00:12:15,133 --> 00:12:16,033
Ma'am.

220
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:19,200
It won't be easy
to get Sir Victor out.

221
00:12:19,333 --> 00:12:23,700
It's the NCIA that caught him.
They have solid evidence.

222
00:12:23,867 --> 00:12:24,933
[MARIANO] Attorney.

223
00:12:26,067 --> 00:12:27,700
Money can solve that.

224
00:12:27,833 --> 00:12:31,533
Look for a greedy agent
in the NCIA.

225
00:12:31,667 --> 00:12:35,633
Slap them with money
just to get Victor out.

226
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:39,000
[LUCAS] Well,
what are you doing?

227
00:12:39,133 --> 00:12:42,000
- Go to my brother!
- [ARTURO] Attorney, let's go.

228
00:12:45,333 --> 00:12:48,333
We lost 100 million pesos

229
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:51,733
because Victor's transaction
in Malaysia did not happen!

230
00:12:51,867 --> 00:12:55,533
Who knows how many more
transactions we lost

231
00:12:55,667 --> 00:12:57,067
because of this incident?!

232
00:12:57,233 --> 00:13:01,167
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

233
00:13:01,267 --> 00:13:03,467
If that lawyer fails,

234
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:05,400
I know another way
we can do this.

235
00:13:06,333 --> 00:13:07,367
What?

236
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:09,733
The woman who arrested Victor...

237
00:13:13,867 --> 00:13:16,467
...is General Ricardo
Jacinto's daughter.

238
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:18,900
Your former chief?

239
00:13:20,233 --> 00:13:21,900
He wasn't just my boss.

240
00:13:23,967 --> 00:13:26,033
We have a deep history.

241
00:13:27,967 --> 00:13:30,833
And I know a lot more about him.

242
00:13:31,733 --> 00:13:38,733
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

243
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:49,667
[RICARDO EXHALES]

244
00:13:52,467 --> 00:13:53,833
[OBJECTS THUDDING]

245
00:13:53,967 --> 00:14:00,933
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

246
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:07,800
[PHONE RINGING]

247
00:14:09,933 --> 00:14:11,433
Hello? Who is this?

248
00:14:11,567 --> 00:14:13,967
It's Mariano. Mariano Zafra.

249
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:18,133
You wouldn't have called
if it's not important.

250
00:14:19,167 --> 00:14:20,533
What do we have to discuss?

251
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:23,933
You probably know
why I called.

252
00:14:24,067 --> 00:14:26,867
[RICARDO]<i> I heard about your son
</i> from last night's news.

253
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,933
My son
whom your daughter arrested!

254
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:31,167
[MARIANO]<i> I have no issue
</i> with you.

255
00:14:31,767 --> 00:14:33,967
We have no issues
with each other.

256
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:36,800
<i>But this might cause a rift
between us, Ricardo.</i>

257
00:14:36,933 --> 00:14:38,000
Are you threatening me?

258
00:14:38,167 --> 00:14:41,000
I don't do threats, Ricardo,
you know that.

259
00:14:41,133 --> 00:14:43,500
I don't know what's going
through my daughter's head.

260
00:14:44,133 --> 00:14:45,667
<i> I don't control her.</i>

261
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:47,833
But I'll see what I can do.

262
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,600
I may have kept obeying you
back then...

263
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:53,000
<i> But that's not the case now.</i>

264
00:14:53,933 --> 00:14:56,467
<i>A lot of things
have changed, Ricardo.</i>

265
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:59,767
You wouldn't want to mess
with someone like me now.

266
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:02,600
[LINE DROPS]

267
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:05,367
[PHONE THUDS]

268
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:10,533
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

269
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:15,367
Lucas?

270
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:16,867
Mama.

271
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,133
Is there any news on Victor?

272
00:15:20,533 --> 00:15:22,467
We're working on it.

273
00:15:24,333 --> 00:15:25,300
But Lucas,

274
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:29,867
while Victor isn't here...

275
00:15:31,733 --> 00:15:34,967
this is your chance to
prove to your dad that

276
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:37,900
you can take care
of our business.

277
00:15:40,200 --> 00:15:43,233
You weren't given
a chance because...

278
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:48,033
your papa only trusts Victor.

279
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:51,000
But I believe,

280
00:15:56,033 --> 00:15:57,500
that you can take care of it.

281
00:15:59,700 --> 00:16:01,633
Now's your chance.

282
00:16:01,733 --> 00:16:08,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

283
00:16:09,067 --> 00:16:10,400
- We need to be ready.
- [TOTO] Ma'am Sam is here!

284
00:16:10,567 --> 00:16:11,700
Ma'am Sam is here!

285
00:16:11,867 --> 00:16:15,000
- [ISOBEL] What?!
- She's here!

286
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:16,900
[ISOBEL] We need
to congratulate her!

287
00:16:17,067 --> 00:16:19,333
Wow, Sam!

288
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:21,167
- [SQUEALS]
- Wow! Sam!

289
00:16:21,267 --> 00:16:22,700
[ISOBEL LAUGHS]

290
00:16:22,867 --> 00:16:24,533
I am so proud of you!

291
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:26,433
- Congratulations!
- [TOTO] Congrats, Ma'am Sam!

292
00:16:26,567 --> 00:16:29,367
You showed the world-- Oh!

293
00:16:29,467 --> 00:16:32,733
The universe, rather,
that you're amazing!

294
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:35,533
Oh, I'm so proud of you!

295
00:16:36,067 --> 00:16:37,367
- Have a seat.
- Wow!

296
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:40,567
- We have a celebration.
- Ma'am! Ma'am!

297
00:16:40,733 --> 00:16:43,000
How did you catch Tiger?

298
00:16:43,133 --> 00:16:45,767
I'm sure you were
like an action star!

299
00:16:45,933 --> 00:16:49,233
She could handle it even
if it was a solo mission.

300
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:51,967
And she could do it all alone!

301
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:54,967
- Right, Sam?
- You're all doing too much.

302
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:56,933
But thank you.

303
00:16:57,267 --> 00:16:59,033
- What is this?
- This is for you, ma'am.

304
00:16:59,133 --> 00:17:03,600
Sweetie, the cake looks good.
Maybe we could slice it?

305
00:17:03,767 --> 00:17:06,133
Why are you so interested
in such a small cake?

306
00:17:06,267 --> 00:17:08,200
And why did you buy
the small one?

307
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:11,367
That's all our budget
could handle!

308
00:17:11,467 --> 00:17:13,600
- It's embarrassing.
- You're all so sweet.

309
00:17:13,767 --> 00:17:15,133
Let's slice it.

310
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:17,933
- [SQUEALS]
- Did you hear that?!

311
00:17:18,033 --> 00:17:20,267
Slice the cake! Slice it now!

312
00:17:20,367 --> 00:17:23,467
[PLATES CLATTERING]

313
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:26,733
Your dad knows about
your achievement.

314
00:17:27,033 --> 00:17:28,767
Ah, what did he say?

315
00:17:29,167 --> 00:17:31,267
I'm sure he's proud of you.

316
00:17:31,433 --> 00:17:34,467
And I told him
to congratulate you.

317
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:42,267
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

318
00:17:45,800 --> 00:17:47,667
Do you want me to bring Gabo?

319
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:50,000
What are your plans for him?

320
00:17:50,167 --> 00:17:52,300
Are you going to give him
another chance?

321
00:17:52,567 --> 00:17:54,967
Find out if...

322
00:17:56,633 --> 00:17:58,767
he nearly caught Victor.

323
00:17:58,867 --> 00:18:01,200
I'll tell your messengers.

324
00:18:06,367 --> 00:18:08,133
I wonder where Gabo is.

325
00:18:08,300 --> 00:18:09,967
Something bad must
have happened there.

326
00:18:10,067 --> 00:18:12,433
Don't worry, nothing bad
will happen to him.

327
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:14,000
What do you mean?

328
00:18:14,167 --> 00:18:16,267
Have you seen
those people earlier?!

329
00:18:16,367 --> 00:18:17,833
They have a lot of guns!

330
00:18:18,633 --> 00:18:19,767
I'm blaming Gabo!

331
00:18:20,333 --> 00:18:24,000
He never told us our enemies
would be big-time people!

332
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:25,333
I'm sure they're loaded.

333
00:18:25,433 --> 00:18:27,667
They had loads of bodyguards
and guns!

334
00:18:27,767 --> 00:18:30,333
I'm worried Gabo won't make it
back here alive.

335
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:31,633
He might be dead!

336
00:18:31,733 --> 00:18:33,667
- Hey!
- Hey, don't say that!

337
00:18:33,833 --> 00:18:35,867
- Stop that!
- [IPE] You shouldn't say that.

338
00:18:36,367 --> 00:18:38,833
He's like a cat.
He won't die easily.

339
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,800
And I'm pretty sure
he won't get caught alive.

340
00:18:43,767 --> 00:18:50,700
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

341
00:18:57,867 --> 00:18:58,867
Hey! Hey!

342
00:18:59,433 --> 00:19:01,000
It's Gabo! He's alive!

343
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:02,000
Gabo!

344
00:19:02,367 --> 00:19:03,367
- Gabo!
- Gabo!

345
00:19:03,467 --> 00:19:04,433
[GASPS]

346
00:19:04,567 --> 00:19:06,033
[TEKLA] Gabo!

347
00:19:06,133 --> 00:19:07,533
[CRYING] Gabo!

348
00:19:07,633 --> 00:19:09,000
We thought something bad
happened to you!

349
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:11,000
Are you hurt? How are you?

350
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:13,533
What happened?

351
00:19:13,633 --> 00:19:14,867
Did you catch Tiger?

352
00:19:14,967 --> 00:19:20,367
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

353
00:19:20,533 --> 00:19:21,867
I caught him.

354
00:19:23,367 --> 00:19:24,867
But a bunch of people came.

355
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:26,833
They shot at me.

356
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:29,733
That's why they got him!

357
00:19:30,767 --> 00:19:32,733
Whoa, Gabo!

358
00:19:33,833 --> 00:19:35,133
We already know your style.

359
00:19:35,267 --> 00:19:37,400
We all live in Tondo.

360
00:19:37,567 --> 00:19:38,800
- Mhm-hmm.
- Maybe you just

361
00:19:38,933 --> 00:19:40,700
took all the money.

362
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:44,433
We all struggled to find Tiger.

363
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:45,933
C'mon, take the money out.

364
00:19:46,333 --> 00:19:48,967
He's right, Gabo.
Where is it?

365
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:52,300
Is that what you think of me?

366
00:19:56,067 --> 00:19:57,433
If you think I got
the reward money,

367
00:19:57,600 --> 00:19:58,900
do you think I'd be here?!

368
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,733
I should've gone straight
to the hospital

369
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:02,100
to pay for my fathers surgery!

370
00:20:02,633 --> 00:20:05,100
You two just don't think,
do you?

371
00:20:05,267 --> 00:20:07,833
Don't compare Gabo to you!
You're all annoying me!

372
00:20:08,467 --> 00:20:09,633
If that's what happened...

373
00:20:10,467 --> 00:20:12,500
then that's a bummer.

374
00:20:13,133 --> 00:20:14,633
You caught him, but he got away!

375
00:20:14,967 --> 00:20:18,267
I am sure the police will
benefit from that.

376
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:20,100
Oh, wait a minute.

377
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:22,767
I think the woman I fought
with at the jewelry store

378
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:24,600
was a police officer!

379
00:20:24,767 --> 00:20:27,267
I've seen her at the bar!
She pushed us, Gabo!

380
00:20:27,367 --> 00:20:29,667
That's why the man she was
with punched you!

381
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:33,633
I'll step on her like a bug
when I see her around!

382
00:20:33,800 --> 00:20:35,933
We went up against big people.

383
00:20:36,067 --> 00:20:39,300
And they look like
an organized syndicate.

384
00:20:39,467 --> 00:20:40,600
[SIGHS]

385
00:20:41,367 --> 00:20:42,700
What will we do, Gabo?

386
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,433
Where will we look for money
to fund Rudy's operation?

387
00:20:46,533 --> 00:20:50,633
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

388
00:20:50,733 --> 00:20:52,300
I don't know.

389
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:55,000
All I know is that...

390
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:59,100
I need to move so they can
start his operation.

391
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:01,867
It's best if we drink to that.

392
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:05,033
We'll find a way to help Rudy.

393
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:07,133
You're right. Hey!

394
00:21:07,633 --> 00:21:08,700
One beer for Gabo!

395
00:21:08,867 --> 00:21:13,333
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

396
00:21:13,667 --> 00:21:14,567
Here.

397
00:21:14,700 --> 00:21:17,800
Have these photocopied
first thing tomorrow.

398
00:21:17,933 --> 00:21:19,367
Make 10 copies.

399
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:22,500
I'll leave early
to solicit money.

400
00:21:22,667 --> 00:21:24,833
- Put it here.
- Okay.

401
00:21:27,333 --> 00:21:28,467
[BETCHAY SIGHS SHARPLY]

402
00:21:32,067 --> 00:21:33,200
[MAMENG] Hey.

403
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,633
Where were you?

404
00:21:36,833 --> 00:21:38,500
I hustled to make money,
what else?

405
00:21:38,667 --> 00:21:39,800
Hmm?

406
00:21:40,567 --> 00:21:42,133
Well, did you make money?

407
00:21:44,267 --> 00:21:45,433
A bit.

408
00:21:46,900 --> 00:21:48,367
Just chump change.

409
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:53,000
You got that illegally, huh?

410
00:21:54,233 --> 00:21:56,667
See? It's annoying, isn't it?

411
00:21:57,633 --> 00:21:59,333
Whatever!
There's my contribution!

412
00:21:59,467 --> 00:22:01,667
Don't tell me
I didn't contribute!

413
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:03,033
Uh, wait, Betchay.

414
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:05,900
Speaking of contributions,
can I...

415
00:22:06,900 --> 00:22:09,667
Can I have some of it
to make copies of these?

416
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:11,333
Take it.

417
00:22:11,433 --> 00:22:13,100
- Really?
- Yeah.

418
00:22:13,733 --> 00:22:15,833
[MAMENG] Take care of that.
That's a huge amount.

419
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:18,967
- [DANTE] Of course. I will.
- Seriously?!

420
00:22:19,100 --> 00:22:22,900
You don't know what I
went through for that.

421
00:22:23,067 --> 00:22:25,267
How could you belittle me?

422
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:27,267
I didn't! I just said
it was a huge amount!

423
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:28,633
I can't believe this!

424
00:22:28,767 --> 00:22:30,533
I said it was a huge amount

425
00:22:30,667 --> 00:22:32,367
- so he should take care of it!
- I should go.

426
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:34,400
You talk as if you're all that.

427
00:22:34,567 --> 00:22:37,033
- [TOTO] Here I go! Here I go!
- Okay!

428
00:22:37,133 --> 00:22:38,933
H-Here-- Here comes Sir Ricardo.

429
00:22:39,067 --> 00:22:40,600
- Oh!
- He's here.

430
00:22:44,567 --> 00:22:45,967
Case closed, Sam?

431
00:22:46,967 --> 00:22:50,367
Ah, yes, Dad.
We caught the suspect.

432
00:22:50,500 --> 00:22:53,000
But we still need
to strengthen the case.

433
00:22:53,133 --> 00:22:55,500
Sam, you don't know
the person you're up against.

434
00:22:55,633 --> 00:22:57,100
He's a powerful man.

435
00:22:57,867 --> 00:22:59,733
Are you sure
about your investigation?

436
00:23:00,633 --> 00:23:03,333
We only had a limited time
to study the case,

437
00:23:03,467 --> 00:23:07,233
but when we got the chance
to arrest the suspect,

438
00:23:07,367 --> 00:23:08,800
we didn't hesitate.

439
00:23:10,433 --> 00:23:12,900
Maybe you were mistaken
about Victor Zafra.

440
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:15,067
I mean, he could've just
been caught in the crossfire

441
00:23:15,200 --> 00:23:17,600
between you and
the real suspect.

442
00:23:17,767 --> 00:23:19,733
Dad, he exchanged fire
with the NCIA.

443
00:23:19,867 --> 00:23:21,667
And he's been doing
illegal transactions.

444
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:22,833
Sam.

445
00:23:23,967 --> 00:23:26,433
The Zafras are operating
legitimate businesses.

446
00:23:26,567 --> 00:23:28,600
What illegal transactions
are you talking about?

447
00:23:28,733 --> 00:23:32,133
Do you have evidence?
Did you find contraband on him?

448
00:23:32,300 --> 00:23:34,133
No, they managed
to take it away.

449
00:23:34,300 --> 00:23:36,100
Then maybe you caught
the wrong guy!

450
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:37,700
[SAM] That's impossible, Dad!

451
00:23:37,833 --> 00:23:40,000
He has an existing murder case!

452
00:23:40,133 --> 00:23:42,267
And he's the leader
of the gold-smuggling syndicate!

453
00:23:43,467 --> 00:23:45,500
Hang on.
Are you defending him?

454
00:23:45,633 --> 00:23:47,433
I'm not defending Victor Zafra!

455
00:23:47,567 --> 00:23:51,267
I'm just asking what you
and your agency did!

456
00:23:51,400 --> 00:23:52,800
Wait, Dad.

457
00:23:52,967 --> 00:23:55,667
We studied this case properly
and followed due process.

458
00:23:55,833 --> 00:23:59,133
The NCIA was able to arrest
a criminal because of me.

459
00:23:59,267 --> 00:24:03,300
I believe I did my job
the best way I know how.

460
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:04,900
Are you really
questioning me on this?

461
00:24:05,033 --> 00:24:07,200
Is that wrong in your eyes too?

462
00:24:07,333 --> 00:24:08,300
Sam!

463
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:10,900
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

464
00:24:11,033 --> 00:24:12,300
Stop it.

465
00:24:12,400 --> 00:24:14,000
You better listen to Dad.

466
00:24:14,167 --> 00:24:16,533
Stop insisting you're right.

467
00:24:18,333 --> 00:24:25,200
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

468
00:24:29,633 --> 00:24:31,767
Max, you better
talk to your sister.

469
00:24:36,233 --> 00:24:37,833
You never fail to impress me.

470
00:24:38,533 --> 00:24:41,200
Not only did you forget
to congratulate your daughter,

471
00:24:42,267 --> 00:24:45,867
you even questioned her
for arresting a criminal.

472
00:24:46,567 --> 00:24:48,533
Is it wrong of me
to give her the right advice?

473
00:24:48,700 --> 00:24:51,533
Advice? You made it seem
like she's done nothing right!

474
00:24:51,700 --> 00:24:54,233
Like everything she does
is wrong!

475
00:24:55,033 --> 00:24:56,100
Isobel.

476
00:24:56,933 --> 00:24:58,333
This is the real world.

477
00:24:58,467 --> 00:25:01,167
That's not how an honorable
law enforcer should act!

478
00:25:01,267 --> 00:25:02,667
There it is.

479
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:05,200
It all comes down
to the same thing with you.

480
00:25:05,300 --> 00:25:08,367
You always talk about honor and
how you were a great general.

481
00:25:08,467 --> 00:25:10,533
How the police force
looked up to you.

482
00:25:10,633 --> 00:25:15,133
Ricardo, for once, forget
that you're a former general.

483
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:18,200
Just be a father!

484
00:25:18,333 --> 00:25:25,300
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

485
00:25:34,167 --> 00:25:35,933
[DOOR OPENS]

486
00:25:36,100 --> 00:25:37,133
[DOOR THUDS]

487
00:25:38,167 --> 00:25:39,400
What was that about?

488
00:25:40,100 --> 00:25:42,233
Why are you asking me?
Ask Dad.

489
00:25:42,333 --> 00:25:43,733
He thinks I'm wrong again.

490
00:25:43,833 --> 00:25:46,167
Am I wrong for doing
my job right?

491
00:25:46,300 --> 00:25:48,900
You talked back at him.
Do you think that's right?

492
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:50,900
Don't do that again,
especially when I'm here.

493
00:25:51,033 --> 00:25:53,067
Am I wrong for
defending myself?

494
00:25:53,167 --> 00:25:54,500
It's not like
I disrespected Dad.

495
00:25:54,633 --> 00:25:56,900
I was just telling him
the truth.

496
00:25:57,000 --> 00:26:00,067
Dad sees something
that we don't, Sam.

497
00:26:00,167 --> 00:26:02,467
We're just new cops.
He's a former chief of police.

498
00:26:02,600 --> 00:26:05,133
He knows a lot about cases
and criminals.

499
00:26:05,267 --> 00:26:07,333
Please learn to listen
to him.

500
00:26:07,467 --> 00:26:10,400
Am I wrong for defending
myself?

501
00:26:10,567 --> 00:26:11,933
That's what I'm asking.

502
00:26:12,067 --> 00:26:14,533
Am I wrong for
solving the case?

503
00:26:14,667 --> 00:26:16,367
Fine. You want to know
what's wrong?

504
00:26:16,500 --> 00:26:18,533
Let's start with that agency
of yours.

505
00:26:18,667 --> 00:26:19,933
Your team should've
coordinated with us.

506
00:26:20,033 --> 00:26:23,133
We're the ones handling Zafra's
case, but you took it from us.

507
00:26:23,300 --> 00:26:25,167
Why are you blaming
my team?

508
00:26:25,300 --> 00:26:28,367
It's not our fault that NLEA
is slow at solving cases.

509
00:26:28,500 --> 00:26:32,000
My team and I caught
a big-time criminal.

510
00:26:32,133 --> 00:26:34,933
Yeah, right!
You're so good at your job!

511
00:26:36,300 --> 00:26:38,633
You never listen, Sam!

512
00:26:38,800 --> 00:26:40,267
In case you forgot,

513
00:26:40,367 --> 00:26:43,967
our family got ruined because
of your stubbornness!

514
00:26:45,067 --> 00:26:50,167
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

515
00:26:50,333 --> 00:26:52,800
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

516
00:26:55,067 --> 00:26:57,300
[DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

517
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:10,900
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

518
00:27:15,500 --> 00:27:18,900
<i>The police fear me and they
follow all my orders.</i>

519
00:27:19,067 --> 00:27:20,500
<i> My word is the law.</i>

520
00:27:20,600 --> 00:27:22,167
<i> I can't let this pass,</i>

521
00:27:22,300 --> 00:27:26,367
<i>even if it means going
against my daughter.</i>

522
00:27:27,300 --> 00:27:34,333
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

523
00:27:48,767 --> 00:27:55,733
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

524
00:28:06,667 --> 00:28:08,800
It's payback time!

525
00:28:08,933 --> 00:28:12,233
<i>Find the guy who
attacked our group.</i>

526
00:28:12,333 --> 00:28:15,133
<i>It's his fault that I'm here
in jail.</i>

527
00:28:15,267 --> 00:28:18,300
And it must be paid
with life.

528
00:28:18,433 --> 00:28:21,433
<i>Bring him to me. He has to
pay for what he did to Victor.</i>

529
00:28:21,567 --> 00:28:22,700
Will you give up
your principles...

530
00:28:22,867 --> 00:28:25,233
<i>Are you going to let
your father die</i>

531
00:28:25,367 --> 00:28:26,667
<i> and not get surgery?</i>

532
00:28:26,833 --> 00:28:29,000
<i>I almost sold my soul
for him.</i>

533
00:28:29,133 --> 00:28:30,400
...for something you need?

534
00:28:30,533 --> 00:28:33,567
<i>We need money!
That's what we need!</i>

535
00:28:33,700 --> 00:28:36,600
<i>I'm here to offer assistance
for Mister Rudy.</i>

536
00:28:36,700 --> 00:28:38,567
Which will Gabo choose?

537
00:28:38,700 --> 00:28:40,167
<i>You can't put an amount
on my father!</i>

538
00:28:40,300 --> 00:28:41,967
<i>We'll make sure the person
who did that to my father</i>

539
00:28:42,100 --> 00:28:43,567
<i> will go to jail!</i>

540
00:28:43,700 --> 00:28:45,500
<i>Sir, what about my
possible suspension?</i>

541
00:28:45,667 --> 00:28:50,067
<i>The board will decide on
whatever you deserve.</i>

542
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:54,267
<i>Our mission would've gone
smooth if not for that guy.</i>

543
00:28:54,367 --> 00:28:56,667
<i>Who is he anyway?
Was he the guy who kissed you?</i>

544
00:28:56,867 --> 00:28:58,367
<i> I'm only sure about one thing.</i>

545
00:28:58,533 --> 00:29:02,100
<i>I want to meet that guy
so I can arrest him.</i>
